{
  "_readme": "Source of truth for which demo surfaces require a signed-in user. Hand-authored, NOT generated. A level is the auth needed to REACH the surface — send the chip, open the linked page — not the strictest thing reachable from inside it (a public learning page may still hold a button that needs a session). Levels: public = works signed out; user = needs a customer session; admin = needs an admin token. `npm run authz:verify` fails if a use case is missing here, if a level is unknown, if a use case is more public than the route it links to, if the BFF guest allowlist drifts from publicAgentActions, or if any route's level disagrees with the guard App.js actually applies.",
  "_readmeRoutes": "`routes` covers every <Route> in demo_api_ui/src/App.js and routes/EducationRoutes.js, seeded from the guards those files already enforce (so adopting this file changed no behavior). The guards stay written inline — RequireAdminLogin renders an 'Log in as admin?' prompt rather than redirecting, and that UX is deliberate — but authz:verify parses the JSX and fails when a guard and this file disagree, so neither side can move alone. Wildcard mounts (`*`, `/setup/*`) are omitted; their children are the addressable surfaces. `softAuthRoutes` are pages whose element reads `user` but renders for everyone (personalized, not gated) — declared public, listed explicitly so the exemption is visible rather than silent.",
